# Browser
# Nature's Rhythm's harmonize cost {X}{G}{G}{G}{G} has no generic mana until X is announced, and the creature to tap is chosen
# before X is (CR 702.180b, 601.2b): the dock must not say tapping Llanowar Elves takes 0 off, or exactly its power, but up to
# its power - "Tap it (up to -1)". With X = 1 the Elves really take the {1} off (CR 702.180a): three Forests and Mox Emerald
# pay {G}{G}{G}{G}, and the Birds of Paradise (mana value 1) is found.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Nature's Rhythm
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Birds of Paradise
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Nature's Rhythm.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Search(Llanowar Elves)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Graveyard.Nature's Rhythm.Cast(X: 1; Ability: Harmonize)
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Nature's Rhythm: tap up to one untapped creature you control to reduce the cost by generic mana equal to its power
Bot1.Choose(Llanowar Elves)
? Client.Bot1.Confirm = Tap it (up to -1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Search(Birds of Paradise)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Nature's Rhythm
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Birds of Paradise.Tapped = false
